    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8068-a519-fefedcf7bc81",
      "type": "text",
      "richText": [
        [
          "In Spring Boot, "
        ],
        [
          "Maven",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " and "
        ],
        [
          "Gradle",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " are tools used to "
        ],
        [
          "build",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " your Java application—this means compiling code, managing libraries (dependencies), packaging into a "
        ],
        [
          ".jar",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " file, and even running or deploying your app. The "
        ],
        [
          "spring-boot-maven-plugin",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ],
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " (or its Gradle counterpart) automates many Spring Boot-specific tasks like running the app, creating executable jars, and more."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80c3-878d-f962e9414572",
      "type": "quote",
      "richText": [
        [
          "💡 Think of it like this: Maven is your build-and-run command center. It knows where your source code is, which libraries you need, and how to turn it all into something runnable."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8056-ba8b-ec19d3ae6ce4",
