        [
          "✅ Best Practices:"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80e0-9709-c762bbff047d",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Keep your "
        ],
        [
          "pom.xml",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " organized and dependencies clean."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80d0-a0e8-c965050d9ac4",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Use "
        ],
        [
          "mvn clean",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " before "
        ],
        [
          "install",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " to avoid stale builds."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80f3-b4e3-d242c51f617c",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Use the plugin to create a fat jar for easy deployment."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-803b-9b65-ef12b89e1a9b",
      "type": "sub_sub_header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "❌ Common Pitfalls:"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-803a-ac4a-e9ac62d9a5fa",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Forgetting to include the plugin—Spring Boot won’t build correctly."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80b6-91d7-ee9882b16b05",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Mixing versions of Spring Boot libraries manually (instead of using the parent "
        ],
        [
          "spring-boot-starter-parent",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          ")."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80f0-9f17-e0e0c37c3870",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Ignoring dependency bloat—too many or unnecessary dependencies can cause conflicts."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80c9-b369-e305f7acd340",
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8003-9a26-fe66f6b32d1f",
      "type": "sub_header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "6. Connection to Other Concepts",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80a8-94a0-c0379642ca08",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Spring Boot Starters",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          ": The plugin works with "
        ],
        [
          "spring-boot-starter-*",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " libraries to package and run them easily."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8092-989a-d75159291ec5",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Auto-Configuration",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          ": When you run the app with the plugin, Spring Boot auto-configures beans (think of them as service objects) behind the scenes."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80d8-8fa8-daed627a828f",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Spring Boot Devtools",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          ": Works well with the Maven plugin for hot-reload support."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-803b-9e86-e82ef3ea7e8a",
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80be-a968-e31ed9060127",
      "type": "sub_header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "7. Quick Interview Answers",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-806e-b0c5-d4c3fa6648a1",
      "type": "quote",
      "richText": [
        [
          "🧠 Q: What is the spring-boot-maven-plugin, and why is it used?"
        ]
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80c2-a6b9-d3fb3b74fddb",
          "type": "text",
          "richText": [
            [
              "A:",
              [
                [
                  "b"
                ]
              ]
            ],
            [
              " It's a Maven plugin that simplifies building and running Spring Boot applications. It allows you to run the app directly using "
            ],
            [
              "mvn spring-boot:run",
              [
                [
                  "c"
                ]
              ]
            ],
            [
              " and also packages the app into a fat jar with all dependencies, so it can be deployed or run anywhere without installing anything else."
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-806a-9c26-ff9c097bea2e",
      "type": "quote",
      "richText": [
        [
          "🧠 Q: What is the difference between mvn install and mvn spring-boot:run?"
        ]
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80d5-8a28-f8e2c49c5727",
          "type": "text",
          "richText": [
            [
              "A:",
              [
                [
                  "b"
                ]
              ]
            ],
            [
              " "
            ],
            [
              "mvn install",
              [
                [
                  "c"
                ]
              ]
            ],
            [
              " compiles the code and packages it into a jar file, saving it to your local Maven repository. "
            ],
            [
              "mvn spring-boot:run",
              [
                [
                  "c"
                ]
              ]
            ],
            [
              " skips the packaging step and runs the app directly from your source files—useful during development."
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8094-b30b-c067ed508635",
      "type": "quote",
      "richText": [
        [
          "🧠 Q: How does Spring Boot run without an external server?"
        ]
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8062-8a33-dde92f523e0d",
          "type": "text",
          "richText": [
            [
              "A:",
              [
                [
                  "b"
                ]
              ]
            ],
            [
              " The Spring Boot Maven plugin packages the application with an embedded web server (like Tomcat or Jetty) inside the jar, so the app runs standalone without needing to install a server separately."
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8086-8fee-c84c700f45bf",
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "id": "ed-build-phases",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Maven phases and starter versions"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ed-build-phases-b0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "The Maven lifecycle orders phases. test runs tests; package produces the artifact; verify includes checks after packaging; install also copies the artifact into the local Maven repository."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ed-build-phases-b1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "The Maven wrapper uses the project’s selected Maven version. It still needs a compatible Java installation."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ed-build-phases-b2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Let the Spring Boot dependency-management platform select compatible versions for its starters. Adding an unrelated starter version can break that alignment."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ed-build-phases-b3",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "The course repository uses Boot 2.7.16 but pins one MongoDB starter to a Boot 3 release. That source choice is not a dependency setup to copy into a new project."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ed-build-phases-b4",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Use dependency:tree when a classpath problem may come from competing versions. An artifact downloading successfully does not prove it is compatible."
        ]
      ]
    }
  ],
